     "assumptions": [
      "ASM-1 and ASM-11 conflict on routing. This spec follows ASM-1: paths are mapped as written (/me), UsePathBase(\"/api\") lets /api/me answer too, and the generated document declares server /api. Mapping under an /api route group (ASM-11) would put /api/me into the document's paths and break conformance with the contract.",
      "ASM-3 ('system starts empty') is overridden by Q-5 and Q-8: the schema is created and a few sample rows are seeded at startup, but only when the database is empty.",
      "Other members exist only as booked and waitlist counts on the session (Q-4). The returned bookedCount and waitlistCount include the demo member. The demo member's waitlist position is stored on their booking row; promotion notices are stored as promoted-at and notice-acknowledged fields on the booking (Q-7).",
      "Precedence of createBooking checks: not_found → cancelled_by_studio → class_has_started → outside_booking_window → already_booked → class_full → overlap → limit_reached. joinWaitlist: not_found → cancelled_by_studio → class_has_started → outside_booking_window → already_booked → not_full. The contract lists the codes but gives no order.",
      "Window boundaries are inclusive for allowed actions: a class can be booked when it starts at most 7 days and at least 15 minutes from now. Cancelling is late when the class starts less than 2 hours from now. Undo is allowed when now − createdAt ≤ 5 seconds. A class has started when now ≥ startsAt.",
      "The overlap check uses half-open intervals [startsAt, endsAt): back-to-back classes do not overlap. Only Booked records for sessions that are not studio-cancelled and have not ended count toward overlap; only Booked records for classes not yet started count toward the limit of 10. Waitlist joins are not checked for overlap or the limit.",
      "The contract's examples disagree on availabilityLabel ('2 spots left' vs 'Only 2 left'). This spec uses: 1 → '1 spot left', 2–3 → 'Only N left', ≥4 → 'N spots left'. The label for a full class with nobody waiting is a draft conflict (REQ-8 vs REQ-9).",
      "Promotion ignores the overlap and limit rules (ASM-5, ASM-15), so skipReason is always null in this release.",
      "A Booked or Waitlisted record on a studio-cancelled session is reported with status and badge 'Cancelled by studio' and appears in the Past list. Booked/Waitlisted records for classes that have started but not ended stay in Upcoming with canChange false. Waitlisted records whose class has ended appear in neither list. All Cancelled records appear in Past, whatever their class time.",
      "Duplicate-booking protection is the already_booked check inside the same request or transaction. No unique index or locking is added (ASM-8, ASM-16).",
      "Build-time OpenAPI generation is detected when the app runs under the GetDocument.Insider tool, so startup database work can be skipped.",
      "All times in messages are 24-hour Europe/London; the cancel confirmation uses \"today HH:mm\" when the class is on the current London day and \"ddd HH:mm\" otherwise. startsAt/endsAt are serialised as UTC ISO-8601.",
      "DaySummary.hasSessions ignores the type/intensity/timeOfDay filters.",
      "currentStreakWeeks counts back from the current London week; if the current week has no Attended record yet, counting starts from the previous week instead of returning 0.",
      "Rule tests run against a temporary SQLite file through WebApplicationFactory with a fake TimeProvider injected (ASM-9, ASM-14); tests may insert session and booking rows directly to set up a state."
